go-media-metadata

Test data
---------

Most test files are generated by the tests themselves (see
internal/bmff/testbuild): synthetic ISO base media files whose "image data"
is random bytes. No third-party sample files are included.

Sample files, each with its source and licence:

testdata/imageio/a-orientation1.heic
testdata/imageio/b-orientation6.heic
    A synthetic 640x480 image (a vertical gradient with a red square in
    the top-left corner, drawn with Core Graphics; no photograph), encoded
    as HEIC by Apple ImageIO (CGImageDestination) on macOS 26.6: a with no
    orientation (ImageIO still writes an irot box of 0 degrees), b with
    orientation 6 (irot 270 degrees anticlockwise, and Exif Orientation 6).
    Made for this project by its authors. Dedicated to the public domain
    under CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

testdata/imageio-corpus/*.jpg
testdata/imageio-corpus/*.heic
    A synthetic 64x48 image (a gradient with a red square, drawn with
    Core Graphics; no photograph), written as JPEG and HEIC by Apple
    ImageIO on macOS 26.6 with the metadata make.swift sets. Made for
    this project by its authors. Dedicated to the public domain under
    CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

testdata/iphone/grid-gainmap-orientation6.heic
    A photo taken with an iPhone 12 Pro on iOS 27.2, as the camera wrote
    it: a grid of tiles, a thumbnail and an HDR gain map sharing one irot
    property (orientation 6), and an Exif item. No location data.
    Photographed by the repository owner, dedicated to the public domain
    under CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

testdata/exiftool/*.jpg
    A synthetic 64x48 image (a gradient with a red square, drawn and
    encoded by Go's image/jpeg; no photograph), with metadata written by
    ExifTool 13.44 (see testdata/exiftool/README.md and make.sh). Made for
    this project by its authors. Dedicated to the public domain under CC0
    1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
